vertico NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

This is the news of e8-vertico, the E8 port of vertico.  'C-h P'
shows it under the package's description.


* Changes in vertico 0.1.0

This is the first release, a port of vertico 2.5 with its vertico-sort
extension.  It needs E8 0.3.1 or newer.

** 'vertico-mode' lists completion candidates down the minibuffer.
Every prompt that completes shows them one per line, the first
selected.  Turning it on turns off icomplete's modes and fido's.

** 'C-n' and 'C-p' select the next and previous candidate.
'<down>' and '<up>' do too, 'M-<' and 'M->' go to the first and last,
and 'C-v' and 'M-v' a page on and back.

** 'M-}' and 'M-{' go to the next and previous group.

** 'TAB' puts the selected candidate in the input.
'RET' takes the selected candidate, 'M-RET' takes the input as typed,
and 'M-w' copies the selected candidate.

** Candidates are sorted by history, then length, then name.
'vertico-sort-function' chooses another order, such as
'vertico-sort-history-alpha', 'vertico-sort-length-alpha' or
'vertico-sort-alpha'; 'vertico-sort-override-function' overrides it.

** 'vertico-count' says how many candidates show, 10 by default.

** 'vertico-cycle' makes moving past the last candidate go to the first.

** 'vertico-preselect' says what is selected first.
"first", "prompt", "no-prompt", or "directory", the default.

** 'vertico-scroll-margin' keeps candidates in view around the selected.

** 'vertico-resize' lets the minibuffer shrink as candidates get fewer.

** The list's faces and formats can be changed.
The faces are 'vertico-current', 'vertico-group-title',
'vertico-group-separator' and 'vertico-multiline';
'vertico-count-format' and 'vertico-group-format' say how the count
and group titles read.
